      <scopecontent id="aspace_sc">
         <head>Scope and Contents</head>
         <p>: Collection consists of 25 mounted black and white and color reproductions of 20th century Japanese paintings. Content varies from original photographic prints to reproductions from magazines and other published sources. Some sections have accompanying clippings folders.</p>
      </scopecontent>
      <arrangement id="aspace_arr1">
         <head>Arrangement</head>
         <p>The photographs are arranged alphabetically by individual artist name. The individual artist material is further divided primarily by the location of the work. The individual artist portion is preceded by a general grouping.</p>
      </arrangement>
      <custodhist id="aspace_22560bd60e7c4209c670fdc3d06976aa">
         <head>Custodial History</head>
         <p>This collection was originally stewarded by the Robert B. Haas Family Arts Library at Yale Library. In July 2026, the collection's stewardship was transferred to Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript Library.</p>
      </custodhist>
